{% doc %}
  Free-shipping threshold progress for the cart drawer header.

  One message, one track. The old layout printed the same sentence twice — as a
  label above the bar and again as a pill hanging below the marker — and spent
  82px of container on a 2px line. The pill is gone; the label is the single
  carrier of the number.

  The track and the fill are now different colours. They used to both be
  #56734F, which meant the bar could never actually show progress.

  #first-text / #amount-to-get / #progress-note / #progress-content are dead to
  this snippet but are still queried by the legacy bonus-item code in
  app.bundle.js — and its `me.remove()` call is unguarded, so deleting them
  throws. They stay hidden exactly as they were.

  @example
  {% render 'FreeShippingCartProgress' %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- comment -%}
  Rendered server-side so the header never paints an empty sentence and a
  zeroed bar for the length of the /cart.js round-trip. setShippingProgress()
  then takes over and agrees with these values.

  data-fsp-state picks which half of the slot is visible. The celebration lives
  on a separate `just-unlocked` class that only JS applies, on the crossing
  itself — otherwise every page load with a qualifying cart replays the reward.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign fsp_threshold = settings.min_shipping | default: 1000000
  comment
    Merchandise subtotal, not the post-voucher total — see the matching note in
    refreshCartUI. A voucher must not push the goal backwards.
  endcomment
  assign fsp_total = cart.items_subtotal_price | divided_by: 100
  assign fsp_remaining = fsp_threshold | minus: fsp_total

  assign fsp_pct = fsp_total | times: 100 | divided_by: fsp_threshold
  if fsp_pct > 100
    assign fsp_pct = 100
  endif

  comment
    Floored at 3% so an untouched cart reads as a journey that has started
    rather than a dead rail. This moves the RENDERING minimum only — the
    rupiah figure in the sentence is always the true remainder.
  endcomment
  assign fsp_scale = fsp_pct | at_least: 3 | divided_by: 100.0

  assign fsp_free = false
  if fsp_remaining <= 0
    assign fsp_free = true
    assign fsp_remaining = 0
  endif
-%}

<div
  class="free-shipping-progress"
  data-fsp-state="{% if fsp_free %}earned{% else %}progress{% endif %}"
  data-free-shipping="{{ settings.min_shipping }}"
>
  <div class="free-shipping-progress-container">
    {%- comment -%}
      One 32px slot holding both states, stacked in the same grid cell. The
      height never changes, so crossing the threshold moves nothing below it —
      and the retract choreography the previous version needed disappears.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="fsp-slot">
    <div class="fsp-progress">
    <p class="free-shipping-progress-container-text" id="shipping-progress-text">
      <span id="shipping-progress-label">
        {%- if fsp_free -%}
          <span data-fsp-prefix>{{ 'cart.progress.unlocked' | t }}</span><span class="fsp-amount" data-fsp-amount></span><span data-fsp-suffix></span>
        {%- else -%}
          <span data-fsp-prefix>{{ 'cart.progress_add' | t }} </span><span class="fsp-amount" data-fsp-amount>{{ fsp_remaining | times: 100 | money }}</span><span data-fsp-suffix> {{ 'cart.progress_more' | t }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </span>

      <span id="first-text" style="display:none;">{{ 'cart.progress.only_text' | t }}</span>
      <span id="amount-to-get" style="display:none;"></span>
      <span id="progress-note" style="display:none;">
        {{ 'cart.progress.left_text' | t }}
        <span class="label-note">{{ 'cart.progress.free_delivery_text' | t }}</span>
      </span>
    </p>

    {%- comment -%}
      The rail is decoration; the sentence above carries the information, so it
      is hidden from assistive tech rather than given a progressbar role whose
      bare percentage would need an aria-valuetext to not mislead.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="free-shipping-progress-container-bar" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="progress-track">
        <div class="progress-fill" style="transform: scaleX({{ fsp_scale }});"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      The earned state, persistent. The 1.4s arrival only ever plays once, at
      the crossing — everyone who reloads, reopens the drawer, or comes back
      tomorrow needs to see the benefit without it. Scope, never a rupiah
      figure: real rates here run Rp 15.000 (Bali) to Rp 85.000 (Indonesia
      Timur), so naming the floor would shrink the gift for everyone off Java.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="fsp-earned">
      <span class="fsp-chip">
        <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M8.4 1.7 14.3 7.6a1 1 0 0 1 0 1.4l-5.3 5.3a1 1 0 0 1-1.4 0L1.7 8.4a1 1 0 0 1-.3-.7V2.4a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h5.3a1 1 0 0 1 .7.3Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          <circle cx="4.9" cy="4.9" r="1.05" fill="currentColor"/>
        </svg>
        <span class="fsp-chip-text">{{ 'cart.progress.earned_chip' | t }}</span>
      </span>
    </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Threshold crossings are announced here, not on the running total — the
      amount repaints ~30 times during the count-down and a live region on it
      would machine-gun the screen reader.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <span class="fsp-sr" data-fsp-announce role="status" aria-live="polite"></span>

    <div class="indicator" style="display:none !important;">
      <div class="bar"></div>
    </div>
    <div id="progress-content" class="item-list" style="display:none !important;"></div>
  </div>
</div>
